n    content: Rewrite push handler as single-statement atomic UPDATE with numeric historyId compare and per-historyId dedupe; move watch renewal off relay.heartbeat into a server-boot setInterval daemon; collapse chat-adapter-gmail fanout into gmail/fanout.ts with bounded chains, 60s per-fanout timeout, and full-sync skip.\n    status: pending\n  - id: db-helpers-split\n    content: Split packages/db/src/gmail.ts into packages/db/src/gmail/{accounts,labels,threads,messages,attachments,search,sync-state}.ts. All upserts become onConflictDoUpdate. queryThreads/searchThreads route through gmail_thread_labels and gmail_messages_fts. Delete dead helpers (getThreadById, listAllThreads, getUnprocessedThreadIds, listMessagesByAccount, listAttachmentsByMessageIds, listAttachmentsByAccount).\n    status: pending\n  - id: router-rewrite\n    content: Update packages/api/src/routers/{gmail,gmail-sync,relay}.ts. Drop dead procedures (getFilterSuggestions, getKnownContacts, getProfile; verify searchThreads consumers first). Flatten getSyncProgress shape. heartbeat becomes a thin connection bookkeeping mutation.\n    status: pending\n  - id: web-progress-shape\n    content: Update apps/web/src/components/google-account-row.tsx to consume the flat getSyncProgress shape. Verify other Gmail UI files compile without changes.\n    status: pending\n  - id: delete-old-modules\n    content: Delete gmail-sync.ts, gmail-client.ts, gmail-extraction.ts, gmail-browse.ts, gmail-push.ts, gmail-watch.ts, relay-client.ts under packages/api/src/lib. Trim packages/chat-adapter-gmail/src/index.ts to envelope schemas + decodeGmailPushPayload only. Update all imports.\n    status: pending\n  - id: tests-and-typecheck\n    content: Port plan + client tests; add mime/history/checkpoint/push/batch tests. Run bun check-types until green. Spot-check backfill row counts (gmail_thread_labels vs json_array_length(labels)).\n    status: pending\nisProject: false\n---\n\n# Full Rewrite: Gmail Subsystem\n\n## 1. Goals\n\n- One Gmail HTTP client. Every call rate-limited. Every error a `GmailApiError`.\n- One MIME builder. RFC 2047 / quoted-printable / multipart-alternative aware.\n- One sync orchestrator. Streaming pagination, batched thread GETs, in-place label deltas.\n- Normalized labels + SQLite FTS5. No more `LIKE '%...%'` and no more `EXISTS (json_each(...))`.\n- Tombstone-aware checkpoint. A single 404 must not stall the mailbox forever.\n- Idempotent push processing. Race-free upserts. Background watch renewal.\n- Drop dead schema, dead db helpers, dead tRPC procedures, dead `chat-adapter-gmail` surface.\n\nNon-goals: app-level features (workflows, agent tools, UI redesign). Workflow/agent-tool plumbing is preserved; only its MIME/HTTP path consolidates.\n\n## 2. New architecture\n\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    PubSub[Google Pub Sub] -->|HTTPS push| Relay[apps/relay]\n    Relay -->|WS gmail.push| API[apps/server tRPC]\n    API --> Push[gmail/push.ts]\n    Push --> Orchestrator[gmail/sync/orchestrator.ts]\n    Orchestrator --> Plan[gmail/sync/plan.ts]\n    Orchestrator --> History[gmail/sync/history.ts]\n    Orchestrator --> Full[gmail/sync/full.ts]\n    Orchestrator --> Checkpoint[gmail/sync/checkpoint.ts]\n    History --> Client[gmail/client.ts]\n    Full --> Batch[gmail/batch.ts]\n    Batch --> Client\n    Client --> RateLimit[gmail/rate-limit.ts]\n    RateLimit --> GmailAPI[Gmail API]\n    Orchestrator --> DB[(\"SQLite (normalized labels + FTS5)\")]\n    Watch[gmail/watch.ts daemon] --> Client\n    Web[apps/web] -->|tRPC| API\n    Extraction[gmail/extraction.ts] --> DB\n    Orchestrator -. on success .-> Extraction\n```\n\n\n\n\n\nModule layout under `packages/api/src/lib/gmail/`:\n\n\n```\ngmail/\n  client.ts        single HTTP entry (auth, rate-limit, retries, GmailApiError)\n  batch.ts         multipart/mixed batch helper (max 50 per request)\n  mime.ts          one MIME builder (RFC 2047, RFC 2045 QP, multipart/alternative)\n  parse.ts         addressparser-backed From/To parse, html-to-text body\n  rate-limit.ts    token bucket (existing, but every call routes through it)\n  errors.ts        GmailApiError + retry-after parsing\n  push.ts          idempotent push handler (single UPDATE with numeric compare)\n  watch.ts         daemon-backed watch renewal\n  sync/\n    orchestrator.ts  p-limit pool + circuit gate + checkpoint advance\n    plan.ts          pure planning (resumes, intents, mode resolution)\n    history.ts       incremental: apply label deltas in-place; only fetch on messagesAdded\n    full.ts          full sync: streaming page-by-page enqueue\n    checkpoint.ts    single-transaction history-id + sync-state advance\n  extraction.ts    single orchestrator (replaces scoped + full duplicate)\n  fanout.ts        chat-sdk fanout helper (collapsed from chat-adapter-gmail)\n```\n\n\n## 3. Schema (additive migration + backfill)\n\nNew migration `packages/db/src/migrations/0006_gmail_normalized_labels_and_fts.sql`:\n\n- Create `gmail_thread_labels(account_id, thread_id, label, PRIMARY KEY(thread_id, label))` plus index on `(account_id, label)`.\n- Create `gmail_message_labels(account_id, message_id, label, PRIMARY KEY(message_id, label))`.\n- Create `gmail_messages_fts` as `CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE ... USING fts5(subject, body_text, from_email, from_name, to_header, cc_header, content='gmail_messages', content_rowid='rowid')` plus rebuild triggers.\n- Drop `gmail_sync_state` (dead in [packages/db/src/schema/gmail.ts](packages/db/src/schema/gmail.ts):181-205, never read/written).\n- Backfill: `INSERT INTO gmail_thread_labels SELECT account_id, id, value FROM gmail_threads, json_each(labels)` (and similar for messages).\n- Backfill: `INSERT INTO gmail_messages_fts(rowid, ...) SELECT rowid, subject, body_text, from_email, from_name, to_header, cc_header FROM gmail_messages`.\n\nPhase-2 migration (after the rewrite ships) drops the JSON `labels` columns from `gmail_threads` and `gmail_messages`. Not in this rewrite to keep migration reversible during validation.\n\nDB helpers ([packages/db/src/gmail.ts](packages/db/src/gmail.ts)) get replaced by a thin module per concern:\n\n- `db/gmail/accounts.ts`: single-statement `onConflictDoUpdate` upserts.\n- `db/gmail/labels.ts`: bulk upsert via VALUES + `onConflictDoNothing`; helpers operate on the join tables.\n- `db/gmail/threads.ts`: `queryThreads` rewritten to use indexed joins on `gmail_thread_labels`.\n- `db/gmail/messages.ts`: `upsertMessages` becomes a single `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE`. FTS triggers keep the index live without app code.\n- `db/gmail/attachments.ts`: stable upsert keyed on `(message_id, gmail_attachment_id, filename)` instead of delete-then-insert in [packages/db/src/gmail.ts](packages/db/src/gmail.ts):743-767.\n- `db/gmail/search.ts`: `searchThreads` rewritten as `gmail_messages_fts MATCH ?`.\n- `db/gmail/sync-state.ts`: kept (`gmail_fetch_state`, `gmail_analysis_state`, `gmail_sync_failures`); add `getRetryableSyncFailures`-style readers wired into the orchestrator's retry pass (so the dead-letter queue stops being write-only).\n\nDead helpers go away: `getThreadById`, `listAllThreads`, `getUnprocessedThreadIds`, `listMessagesByAccount`, `listAttachmentsByMessageIds`, `listAttachmentsByAccount` (no callers anywhere outside [packages/db/src/gmail.ts](packages/db/src/gmail.ts)).\n\n## 4. Engine rewrite\n\n### `gmail/client.ts`\n\n- One `gmailFetch<T>` covers GET/POST/DELETE for the entire subsystem (replaces both [packages/api/src/lib/gmail-client.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-client.ts):172 and the bypass in [packages/api/src/lib/gmail-browse.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-browse.ts):19-52). Both go away.\n- Token-bucket gate is the only external limiter. Removes the lopsided coverage.\n- Built-in transient retry on 5xx with jittered backoff before surfacing to the orchestrator's circuit.\n- 404 returns a sentinel (`GmailApiError.isNotFound`) so callers can tombstone instead of erroring.\n\n### `gmail/batch.ts`\n\n- `batchThreadGet(token, ids: string[])` packs up to 50 `GET /users/me/threads/{id}?format=full` into a single `multipart/mixed` POST to `/batch/gmail/v1`. Returns `Array<{id, result: ParsedThread | NotFound | Error}>`.\n- Used by `sync/full.ts` and the `messagesAdded` branch of `sync/history.ts`.\n- `batchModifyMessages(token, {ids, addLabelIds, removeLabelIds})` for `users.messages.batchModify` — exposed to `gmail-agent-tools.ts` so future bulk label operations are one HTTP call.\n\n### `gmail/mime.ts`\n\n- Single `buildMime({from, to, cc, bcc, subject, inReplyTo, references, html, text, attachments})` returns a base64url string.\n- RFC 2047 encoded-word for non-ASCII display names and subject.\n- `multipart/alternative` for text + html (`text` derived from `html` via `html-to-text` when omitted).\n- `quoted-printable` body encoding (replaces `Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit` lie in [packages/chat-adapter-gmail/src/index.ts](packages/chat-adapter-gmail/src/index.ts):384-414).\n- Replaces all three of: `chat-adapter-gmail::buildReplyMime`, `gmail-agent-tools.ts::buildRfc2822Message` + `buildRawMessage` (with the `<pre>` wrap that gets stored forever), and the inline construction in the agent path.\n- `Re:` prefix detection covers `re:`, `aw:`, `r\\u00e9f:`, `rv:`, `sv:`, `vs:`, `wg:`. Locale-tolerant.\n- Reply addressing rule: `Reply-To` if present, else `From`, never the current user (fixes [packages/chat-adapter-gmail/src/index.ts](packages/chat-adapter-gmail/src/index.ts):398).\n\n### `gmail/parse.ts`\n\n- `parseAddress(raw)` uses `addressparser` (nodemailer's small util) covering quoted display names, RFC 2047 encoded names, IDN. Replaces both naive parsers in [packages/api/src/lib/gmail-client.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-client.ts):200-213 and [packages/chat-adapter-gmail/src/index.ts](packages/chat-adapter-gmail/src/index.ts):506-511.\n- `htmlToText` uses `html-to-text` with link-text expansion and `<pre>` preservation. Replaces the regex pipeline in [packages/api/src/lib/gmail-client.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-client.ts):246-258 (which currently drops every URL).\n- `extractBody` becomes container-aware (`multipart/alternative` picks last preferred type; `multipart/mixed` concatenates).\n- `extractAttachments` distinguishes `Content-Disposition: inline` from real attachments.\n\n### `gmail/sync/orchestrator.ts`\n\n- Replace `@tanstack/pacer` `AsyncQueuer` with `p-limit`. Smaller surface; pause/resume becomes a single `Promise<void>` gate.\n- One per-account orchestrator, registered in a `Map<accountId, Orchestrator>` with a per-account async lock that closes the TOCTOU race in [packages/api/src/lib/gmail-sync.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-sync.ts):957-993.\n- Circuit breaker: on 429, the gate is held for `min(retryAfter, MAX_BACKOFF)`. Caps `exactRetryAfter` (currently uncapped at [packages/api/src/lib/gmail-sync.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-sync.ts):892-914).\n- Progress writes are coalesced (every 50 threads or 1s, whichever first). One `incrementFetchProgress` per ~50 instead of per-thread.\n\n### `gmail/sync/plan.ts`\n\n- Pure module, no DB. Same `resolveSyncStartPlan` shape, but the \"push rejected because paused\" bug ([packages/api/src/lib/gmail-sync.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-sync.ts):195-212) is fixed: a paused incremental no longer blocks `push`-intent runs.\n\n### `gmail/sync/full.ts`\n\n- Streaming `listAllThreadIds` becomes an `AsyncIterable<string[]>` of pages. The orchestrator enqueues a page and starts fetching while later pages are still listing. Eliminates the \"100k IDs in memory before queue starts\" wait in [packages/api/src/lib/gmail-client.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-client.ts):317-342.\n- Each page is partitioned into batches of 50 and dispatched through `batchThreadGet`.\n\n### `gmail/sync/history.ts`\n\n- `getHistory(token, startId, types: [\"messageAdded\", \"labelAdded\", \"labelRemoved\", \"messageDeleted\"])` (uses the `historyTypes[]` filter to shrink payloads).\n- Apply `labelsAdded` / `labelsRemoved` directly to `gmail_thread_labels` / `gmail_message_labels`. Zero thread fetches for the dominant change type. Replaces the \"every changed thread re-fetched\" path in [packages/api/src/lib/gmail-sync.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-sync.ts):564-620.\n- Apply `messagesDeleted` as a tombstone (DELETE row + DELETE labels). Replaces the implicit deletion logic in [packages/api/src/lib/gmail-sync.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-sync.ts):380-383.\n- Only `messagesAdded` triggers a `batchThreadGet`.\n- `expired === true` no longer dumps the entire mailbox. Falls back to `q=newer_than:14d` so only recent threads re-sync (Gmail history is at most ~7d, doubled for safety). Beyond that, the local DB is already authoritative for older threads since they cannot have changed.\n\n### `gmail/sync/checkpoint.ts`\n\n- Single transaction: `UPDATE gmail_accounts SET history_id=? ...; UPDATE gmail_fetch_state SET status='completed' ...`. Either both land or neither. Closes the inconsistency window described in the audit.\n- 404 thread fetches are tombstoned and counted as `skipped`, not `failed`. The \"single 404 stalls the checkpoint forever\" failure mode in [packages/api/src/lib/gmail-sync.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-sync.ts):706-724 is gone.\n- Failed (transient) threads are recorded into `gmail_sync_failures`. After every successful incremental, a follow-up retry pass replays unresolved failures (this finally wires the dead readers).\n\n### `gmail/extraction.ts`\n\n- Single `runExtraction(accountId, opts)` replaces both [packages/api/src/lib/gmail-extraction.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-extraction.ts) `GmailExtractionOrchestrator` and the parallel `processScopedThreads`. `opts.scope` is either `\"all_unprocessed\"` or `{ gmailThreadIds: string[] }`.\n- Cancellation honored in both modes (the scoped variant currently ignores it; see [packages/api/src/lib/gmail-extraction.ts](packages/api/src/lib/gmail-extraction.ts):277-322).\n\n### `gmail/push.ts` and `gmail/watch.ts`\n\n- `processGmailPushNotification` becomes a single `UPDATE gmail_accounts SET last_notification_history_id = ? WHERE id = ? AND (last_notification_history_id IS NULL OR CAST(? AS INTEGER) > CAST(last_notification_history_id AS INTEGER))`. Atomic, race-free, replaces the read-then-write at [packages/db/src/gmail.ts](packages/db/src/gmail.ts):144-166.\n- Dedupe by `historyId` in addition to the relay's `messageId` dedupe.\n- `watch.ts`: a `setInterval`-driven daemon registered on app start (lives in `apps/server` boot, not on UI heartbeats). `relay.heartbeat` becomes pure connection bookkeeping; `ensureLocalGmailWatches` is no longer called from a tRPC procedure.\n\n### `gmail/fanout.ts`\n\n- Owns the chat-sdk fanout previously in `chat-adapter-gmail`. Imports `parseMessage` + `encodeThreadId` from `gmail/parse.ts`. Bounded `Map<threadId, Promise>` with a 60s timeout per fanout to prevent the unbounded chain leak in [packages/api/src/lib/chat-gmail.ts](packages/api/src/lib/chat-gmail.ts):147-199.\n- Full sync ingestions skip fanout (only push-driven incrementals fire it). Stops the thundering-herd of chat-sdk `processMessage` calls during initial sync.\n\n`packages/chat-adapter-gmail` shrinks to: `gmailPubSubEnvelopeSchema`, `gmailPushPayloadSchema`, `decodeGmailPushPayload`, `GmailPushPayload`, `GmailPubSubEnvelope` (used by `apps/relay`). All adapter-shaped methods (`postMessage`, `editMessage`, `deleteMessage`, `fetchMessages`, `fetchThread`, `handleWebhook`, `parseMessage`, `encodeThreadId`, `decodeThreadId`) move into `apps/server`'s `gmail/fanout.ts` or get deleted.\n\n## 5. tRPC contract\n\n`packages/api/src/routers/gmail.ts`:\n\n- Drop dead procedures: `getFilterSuggestions`, `searchThreads` (UI doesn't call it; in fact the UI uses `gmail-cache.ts` Google HTTP), `getKnownContacts`, `getProfile`. Confirmed zero apps/web callers.\n- Wait \\u2014 reconsidering: `searchThreads` powers the global command palette per the audit grep, double-check before removal.\n- Keep contract intact for: `getThreads`, `getThread`, `getThreadCount`, `getLabels`, `getLabelCatalog`, `getThreadDrafts`. Internals re-route to normalized labels + FTS, returned shapes unchanged so [apps/web/src/components/inbox/gmail-thread-table.tsx](apps/web/src/components/inbox/gmail-thread-table.tsx), [apps/web/src/components/inbox/gmail-thread-detail.tsx](apps/web/src/components/inbox/gmail-thread-detail.tsx), and friends keep working.\n\n`packages/api/src/routers/gmail-sync.ts`:\n\n- Flatten `getSyncProgress` to `{ phase: \"idle\" | \"fetching\" | \"extracting\" | \"completed\" | \"error\", fetched, fetchTotal, extracted, extractTotal, error, account: { hasCompletedFullSync, needsFullResync } }`. Drops the duplicated full/incremental block since `phase` carries the meaning. UI only consumer is [apps/web/src/components/google-account-row.tsx](apps/web/src/components/google-account-row.tsx) which adjusts in step.\n- `startSync` keeps shape. `cancelSync` keeps shape. `startExtraction` keeps shape.\n- Workflows procedures unchanged (no engine surface).\n\n`packages/api/src/routers/relay.ts`:\n\n- `heartbeat` no longer triggers `ensureLocalGmailWatches` or `triggerPendingGmailNotificationSyncsThrottled`. Both move to a server-boot daemon. The mutation becomes a thin \"ensure WS open\" call.\n\n## 6. apps/web changes\n\n- [apps/web/src/components/google-account-row.tsx](apps/web/src/components/google-account-row.tsx): adjust to new flat `getSyncProgress` shape.\n- [apps/web/src/lib/gmail/types.ts](apps/web/src/lib/gmail/types.ts): unchanged contracts re-import unchanged.\n- All other Gmail consumers (table, columns, row preview, thread detail, draft hooks, label hooks, workflow editor) untouched because their procedure shapes are preserved.\n- Verify [apps/web/src/components/relay-heartbeat.tsx](apps/web/src/components/relay-heartbeat.tsx) still works against the slimmer heartbeat (it ignores the response, so no change needed).\n\n## 